course: dictionary
lesson: 2892
title: Dot: one word, many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A dot is a very small round mark. The same word can also mean other things, so you must read the words around it to know which meaning fits. The clues are your context.
explain: «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint: the black dot in your eye, the pupil, shrinks fast.» Here the clues are eye, pupil and squint, so dot means a small round mark. Try your meaning in the sentence: «the black small round mark in your eye» still makes sense.
explain: Dotted is a different form of the word. «Visit a garden pond in early spring and you may find a clump of frogspawn with hundreds of black dots» tells you that dots means many small marks. The word hundreds is the clue.
fact: A dot is a very small round mark.
fact: «Dot» is also said for the point in a web or email address, like «example dot com».
fact: In maths, a dot can be a decimal point, and rows of dots can show a multiplication: rows × dots in each = total.
fact: «On the dot» means exactly on time.
fact: «Dotted» means with many small marks, or with things scattered here and there.
exercise: «Printed pictures in books and magazines are made of tiny dots of four inks.» What are the dots in this sentence? | Big pictures on a wall | *Very small round marks | Long lines of ink | Holes in the paper
exercise: In a web address, what does the word dot mean? | *The point between parts of the address, said «dot» | Scattered here and there | Exactly on time | A small round mark on a page
exercise: «...frogspawn with hundreds of black dots.» What does dotted mean? | Very late | Round and very large | *With many small marks, or scattered here and there | Hidden under a leaf
test: «Walk out of a dark cinema into bright sunshine and you squint.» What word in the sentence tells you the dot is a small round mark? | Bright | *Pupil | Squint | Walk
test: In maths, what can a dot be? | *A decimal point | A web address | Exactly on time | Scattered here and there
exam: «The children arrived on the dot.» What does «on the dot» mean? | *Exactly on time | Covered in dots | Scattered here and there | A web address
